\pard\sl-240\slmult1 \cf1\lang1033\fs28\f0 The Haunted House\fs24 \par
\cf2 Okay - you finally decided to do it.  For weeks you've been putting it off.  A so called friend of yours bet you that you wouldn't do it, but you're determined to prove them wrong.  At the end of the street where you live, there is a large hill, and at the top sits an old haunted house.  The story is that there is a large chest of gold somewhere in the house, but no-one has ever been brave enough to stay in there long enough to find out. \par
\par
You spent the last day preparing yourself for what may be the biggest and most scary adventure of your life, and for what may be even more important - to prove you're not a coward.\par
\par
After making that lonesome journey up the hill, you reach an ominous looking gate.  You pull it open - the gate making a creaking noise which would wake the dead - step inside the garden, and close the gate behind you.\par
\cf1 \par
shake gutter\par
\cf2 You violently shake the guttering.  Not surprisingly, a piece falls off, and lands with a plop, by your feet.\par
\cf1 \par
take guttering\par
\cf2 You pick up the piece of guttering.\par
\cf1 \par
drop fags\par
\cf2 You drop the packet of fags.\par
\cf1 \par
open door\par
\cf2 You grab hold of the handle, and twist hard.  It obviously hasn't been opened for some time, as it is quite difficult.  With all your might, you finally manage to get the enormous door open.\par
\cf1 \par
in\par
\cf2 You move in.\par
You are standing in the reception area of the house.  To your west is the kitchen.  The main hall is to your north.  To the east, is the conservatory.  The front door leads outside.  High above your head is a fantastic chandelier.\par
\cf1 \par
n\par
\cf2 You move north.\par
You are standing in the main hall.  There is a majestic rug in the centre of the room.  There is a large fireplace here.  There is a small doorway in one of the side walls leading down.  The reception area is to the south.  The dining room is to the north, the study to the east, and there is a spiral staircase leading up.\par
\cf1 \par
